## Pitfall index

- "All gates green, so it works live" → every gate ran on the permissive surface; for a divergence
  class that statement is unsupported.
- A smoke script that asserts a URL form nobody verified against live → it can pin the defect as
  expected (that run, above). Assert the form the code *emits*, and prove that form live.
- "Media renders in Pages, so it will render for visitors" → preview resolves media from the CM;
  live needs the publish.
- Revalidation verified against a local `next start` → single process, single cache; a deployment
  has neither.
- Discovering a divergence and fixing only the call site → also fix the **seam** that let two
  emitters diverge (one canonical helper) and add a guard, or it returns.
- Waiting for `/publish` to reveal the class → that is the live incident, not the check. The point
  of one early live assertion is that it lands before real visitors do.
